# The core loop on a normal new game (seed 1, the default), through the real keys:
# wake by the square, take driftwood, stone and dead wood, lay a fire, make
# charcoal, a haft and a pick at it, meet a machine and find its working side,
# see the night in with the lamp, and walk over the border into a second country.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/core_loop.tour --give=driftwood:6,scrap:1
# (--give tops the creel up so the making does not need twenty trips to the
# strand, and brings one plate from the tip fifty tiles inland.)
shot 01-wake-by-the-square
# The scripted stretch is not a random fight: nothing new comes until the machine is met.
coast calm
# Driftwood on the strand below the village: walk to it, press use. The tour
# names what it takes, so where the strand lays it does not matter.
# The four takes are asked for BY NAME, the way tours/feel.tour asks for the same
# ones. `near KIND` finds the nearest of that kind with work still in it, stands
# in reach and turns to face it, which is the whole of what the four `at X,Y`
# lines here used to arrange by hand. One of them, `at 200,436`, was open SEA: it
# was never a place to stand, only a seed thrown south of the square so that the
# `at prop:driftwood` under it would choose a strand piece. It worked, and the
# rule it broke is the one this repo has already paid for twice.
at prop:driftwood
press use 0.1
await took 3
wait 0.2
shot 02-driftwood-taken
at prop:driftwood
press use 0.1
await took 3
# Dead wood fallen under a broadleaf: `Takes` gives a broadleaf as fell_tree or
# deadfall, and what the key chooses with a knife in hand is the deadfall.
near broadleaf
walk 0,0 0.05
press use 0.1
await took 8
wait 0.2
shot 03-dead-wood
# A loose stone off each of two boulders. `near` will not offer the same one
# twice, which is what the two hand-picked boulders were arranging.
near boulder,stone_ore
walk 0,0 0.05
press use 0.1
await took 14
near boulder,stone_ore
walk 0,0 0.05
press use 0.1
await took 14
wait 0.2
shot 04-stone
# Open ground near the village: the first press asks, the second lays the fire.
# ASKED FOR BY NAME, like the four takes above. `at 188.5,428.5` was a number off
# an old map run, and on this world it is THE CRAGS -- fog and bare terraces most
# of a world away from the coast, where the slate says "lay it on open ground"
# and the press is rightly refused. `ground grass` takes the coast's own
# plain_ground and prefers a tile clear of props, which is what open ground IS.
ground grass
press use 0.1
await fire_asked 2
wait 0.3
shot 05-asked-where
press use 0.1
await made 4
wait 0.5
shot 06-fire-laid with station:fire
# Making at the fire: the page lists what this fire can make.
tap craft
wait 0.6
shot 07-making-page with app:crafting
# Charcoal is set going on the fire and cooks in world time; a haft is whittled meanwhile.
choose charcoal
tap use
wait 0.3
shot 08-charcoal-on-the-fire with station:fire
choose haft
tap use
await made 3
tap pause
wait 0.4
# The clock on to when it is done (a jump, like the teleports); standing at the fire it comes off.
hour 10
await made 4
wait 0.3
shot 08b-charcoal-taken
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose pick_made
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
hour 11
await made 4
wait 0.3
shot 09-a-pick-from-plate
tap craft
wait 0.6
tap pause
wait 0.4
tap inventory
wait 0.6
shot 10-carrying-the-pick with app:inventory
tap inventory
wait 0.4
# Making took the afternoon; the fight is shown in the day it would have been
# met in (a clock jump, like the teleports).
hour 13
# A runner in the field north of the village: met face on, the blow rings off
# its plate and does nothing. `open_coast` is open standable ground clear of
# every village and depot, which is what "a field" was reaching for.
place open_coast
zoom 10
wait 1.0
coast wild
spawn runner
await tell 4
tap dodge
wait 0.3
try 5
walkto mob 1.5
tap swing
await ring 1.5
end
wait 0.04
shot 11-plate-rings with mob:runner
# A watcher stands its ground further on. Its working part is its lens, in
# front: there the blow goes home.
# The same ground as the runner above, which is fine because the `coast calm`
# below clears the bodies — `FightSim.clear_mobs` removes every MobState, the
# dead included. It was `at 160,352`, which sat at blend 0.20: a fight staged in
# a transition band, lit and dressed by two landscapes at once, and nothing in
# the file said so.
coast calm
place open_coast
wait 1.0
spawn watcher
wait 0.5
try 5
walkto mob 2
tap swing
await hit 1.5
end
wait 0.04
shot 12-the-working-side with mob:watcher
tap swing
wait 0.6
tap swing
wait 0.6
shot 13-after-the-fight with body:watcher
coast calm
# Back to the fire as the light goes: the lamp against the dark.
zoom 15
# Back to where the fire was laid, and then AT it: `station:fire` is crafting
# reach (STATION_REACH, edge to edge) and the hard-coded spot need not be inside
# it, while `at prop:fire` alone would walk to whichever fire is nearest — which
# after the fight up the coast is a village one, sixty tiles the other way.
at 189.5,428.5
at prop:fire
hour 21.5
wait 0.6
shot 14-night-at-the-fire with station:fire
press lamp 0.1
wait 0.5
walk -1,-1 1.2
shot 15-lamp-lit with lamp
walk 1,1 1.2
at prop:fire
# Lie down: the press is held long enough to land on a slow frame, and the
# night is AWAITED. This frame was a picture of 22:05 with the footer still
# offering `e fire - sleep`, called "slept to morning" for a year.
# A press made while the hands are still busy is buffered and then dropped, so
# a player presses again: the tour does what the player does.
try 6
press use 0.4
await slept 3
end
wait 0.6
shot 16-slept-to-morning
# North to the border: the land turns and the notebook names it. The border is
# asked for BY NAME (GenPlaces ecotone), the way countries.tour asks for its
# three -- `at 160.5,352.5` was the same stale-number bug as the fire above, and
# it had quietly become moss on the machine_city border.
# The home continent's own border since GEN 24: the bonelands are on another.
place coast-pinewood
wait 0.5
shot 17-the-coast-pinewood-border with border:coast-pinewood
# Loaded with a pick, charcoal, wood and stone, the same walk covers less
# ground than an empty-handed one: the old 4.5 s stopped short of the border
# it is named for.
walk 1,-1 4.5 run
walk 1,-1 3.5 run
wait 1.2
shot 18-into-the-pinewood with land:pinewood
